cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SIFT: code and results"
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, cite both this repository and the
  paper listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tahpnart8/sift"
abstract: >-
  Code, configuration and result tables for SIFT, a diagnostic framework that
  decomposes the performance drop from random to temporal evaluation of a
  ransomware family classifier into four evaluation-protocol confounds plus a
  residual, using an exact Shapley-Shorrocks decomposition over a complete
  16-cell ablation lattice.
keywords:
  - ransomware family classification
  - temporal evaluation
  - dataset shift
  - Shapley decomposition
  - evaluation confounds
# TODO before publishing: add the remaining co-authors, with ORCID where held,
# in the same order as the paper.
authors:
  - family-names: "Tran"
    given-names: "Duc Phat"
preferred-citation:
  type: conference-paper
  title: >-
    SIFT: Decomposing Temporal Performance Degradation in Ransomware Family
    Classification
  year: 2026
  authors:
    - family-names: "Tran"
      given-names: "Duc Phat"
